WEBVTT

00:42:59.046 --> 00:43:02.625
is a massive series of essentially
deep-learning-type algorithms

00:43:02.649 --> 00:43:04.022
going on there.

00:43:04.046 --> 00:43:06.680
And that as we continue
to connect the dots here,

00:43:06.704 --> 00:43:08.383
that it may be possible to assemble

00:43:08.407 --> 00:43:10.999
some kind of general
intelligence from that?

00:43:12.180 --> 00:43:16.656
KFL: I think anything is possible,
but I think it's quite unlikely.

00:43:16.680 --> 00:43:19.902
Because if you just say
that theoretically,

00:43:19.926 --> 00:43:22.315
everything can be built from parts,

00:43:22.339 --> 00:43:25.403
we could say that when
we have transistors,

00:43:25.427 --> 00:43:27.090
that's enough to build everything.

00:43:27.114 --> 00:43:30.212
Or when Alan Turing
invented the Turing machine,